ence i promised him i'd  make good  i have been honest for over 30 years  but very lonesome but i want it  understood but the voice of the land  that it doesn't pay really and truly to  be abandoned  i don't think it pays to violate the law  in any sense  i hope under circumstances by speaking  to the public  that i may in some small way assist  the better understanding of law  enforcement i have no reference to  prohibition  i speak of the law in general and now i  want to say for the benefit of the boys  of the land  don't rob anybody don't think of  violating the law  i want you to realize that all the  misery and the heartache  that was incident to those days of  outlawing  come back to me like a cruel shadow  i want to see the law enforced i want  the law to be enforced honestly on  all alike in this land of ours so that  every  void now growing up under its influence  can have respect  and will obey the law instead of being  thrown into a vortex  that we have now like the crime  commission is trying to suppress  i want to see your boys going to schools  and to colleges  growing up to be men and not bandits  but if they've got to violate the law  let them become  uh wait and become candidates for public  office  they can get it so much easier and not  be caught  i thank you very much  [Music]  do  you
 

